A||N||18||chrissherman||seized 2.5 from siting with the pluges out||||5||
Z||000000||chrissherman||12-02-2000||09:42 PM||||Got the clutch master cylender working Now I find out the car has ben siting for 9 mounths with the pluges out and is seized up what do I put in the cylender's To free it up??? I am going to put azatone in the cyl's to get the moister out of thear then marvel oil/ atf/and silacone sprayand maybe some teflon treatment as well Then try rocking the car in gear but what gear to rock it in????1st 2nd 3rd or4th thank's chris<P>[This message has been edited by chrissherman (edited 12-02-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by chrissherman (edited 12-03-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by chrissherman (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||12-02-2000||10:26 PM||||The best solution is to replace them with new  GM ones. People have not had very good luck trying to repair flakey hydraulic components. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-02-2000||10:29 PM||||Put Marvel Mystery Oil in there, let it sits, put some more, then try cranking!  Lot of people on here will swear by it.||||reg||3
Z||000003||JohnnyK||12-03-2000||01:33 AM||||Hydraulics? Anyways, I would suggest lubing them up real good (with whatever you want) and then putting a socket on the engine (the main pullet) and cranking it slowly and see how that goes. I would not try cranking it right away. Things could go wrong (they always do).||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||12-03-2000||01:56 AM||||Use whatever you can thing of to soften the rust. (mix up different kinds) You will need to let it set for a while (days!) If you try to force it there is a possibility that the rings will break or the ring grooves on the pistons or both. TAKE YOUR TIME! Make sure to fill the cylinders full till whatever you put in there runs out the top. I've been able to free up a couple this way, hopefully there wasn't liquid in them which may have had an opportiniuty to freeze. Be cautious of the clutch, I doubt that it will work properly due to it's previous condition as the bore in one or both cylinders are pitted. (allows fluid to pass between the seals.)<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||chrissherman||12-03-2000||02:16 AM||||JohnnyK I dont want to snap off the bolt on the crank pully||||reg||1
Z||000006||chrissherman||12-03-2000||02:24 AM||||Indianda_rest_guy the slave and master boure's are smouth and clean P.S. THANK'S GUY'S chris sherman||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||12-03-2000||01:43 PM||||You shouldn't snap it (well, you should know when to stop.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> You also don't want to total your starter either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||StuGood||12-03-2000||02:37 PM||||Since I have almost no experience freeing up seized engines, I'll pipe in and tell you what I'd probably do  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  The following assumes you have already marinated the engine overnight (or however long) with some kind of solvent/lubricant, and have taken steps to free up the engine.  <P>Jack up/ make sure the rear wheels turn freely (in case the rear e-brake might be hung up).  Lower car to the ground.<P>Put the car in the highest gear (4th), and try moving the car. That will give you you the most leverage, and will cause the engine to turn the slowest.  If it won't turn forwards, try moving the car backwards a little (might unloose something, like a stuck starter drive). Don't go overboard -  if the engine is <B>really</B> seized, the next weak link in the driveline might be something expensive  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> !      <P>Hope this helps some  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||theogre||12-03-2000||03:01 PM||||Criss, I think the bolt in the crank is Grade 8 or better. What ever it is, If you snap it the motor was shot. It doesn't take that much force to spin a good one with a wrench. Infact usually the problem with getting that bolt out is trying to keep the enigne from turning.<P>If the walls of the cylinders are rusted the engine will in all likelyhood need to be fully rebuilt. DO NOT use acetone in the engine. Use marvel or whatever oil and let it soak.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||bubbajoexx||12-04-2000||07:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chrissherman:<BR><B>Got the clutch master cylender working Now I find out the car has ben siting for 9 mounths with the pluges out and is seized up what do I put in the cylender's To free it up??? I am going to put azatone in the cyl's to get the moister out of thear then marvel oil/ atf/and silacone sprayand maybe some teflon treatment as well Then try rocking the car in gear but what gear to rock it in????1st 2nd 3rd or4th thank's chris<P><BR>[This message has been edited by chrissherman (edited 12-02-2000).]<P><BR>[This message has been edited by chrissherman (edited 12-03-2000).]<P><BR>[This message has been edited by chrissherman (edited 12-03-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>yah chriss the best way to unsiez a engine is to use an oil can filled with brake fluid  squit about 8 squirts into each plug hole let it set for about an hour then turn the engine over with the plugs out the brake fluid will desolve the rust in the cylinders  you may have to try twice but it will work ive done plenty of siezed motors bubbajoexx<BR>||||reg||1
